ed to id Software.","src","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/three-quake-claude-port.webp","alt","Quake’s shareware level rendered in the Three.js port, with a first-person weapon and the original status bar.","https://mrdoob.github.io/three-quake/","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","GameMap browser capture","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)","items",[80],"Claude model / chat","links","Related resources",[86],"resourceIds","section",{"_57":87,"_25":88},"Three.js","/resources/threejs/","Creator evidence",[92],"evidence",{"_57":93,"_25":94,"_95":96},"Read the author’s AI and original-game credits","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake#credits","note","The maintainer distinguishes id Software’s original game from the Three.js port made with Claude assistance.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[101],{"_57":102,"_25":103,"_95":104},"Open the complete browser port","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake","Complete browser port, maps, runtime source and tests, with the shareware pak0.pak. Code is GPL-2.0; original Quake game data has separate terms and is not relicensed by the code license.","Access type","playable","demo","Play or run",[110],{"_57":111,"_25":68,"_95":112},"Play Three Quake","Keyboard, mouse and a WebGL-capable browser. The included shareware data covers Episode 1; full-game content is separate.","Game platform","Browser","Guide format","disclosure","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[120],{"_57":121,"_25":122,"_95":-7},"Read the port credits and creator dev log","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake#dev-log","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[127,128,129,130],"Open the browser build, start a new single-player game and test the movement and firing controls.","Read the creator’s port credits and dev log alongside the original id Software source reference.","Inspect the browser renderer, game runtime, maps and tests to trace how the existing game was adapted.","Use the included shareware data for Episode 1; a registered full-game data set is separate and must be supplied by its owner.","AI workflow / foundation context","Mr.doob credits Claude for assistance with the Three.js port. Quake’s game design and original implementation belong to id Software; this is an AI-assisted port, not a claim that AI created Quake. The README links a creator dev log without identifying a particular Claude client.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","3D","track","metadata","Engine","Three.js · JavaScript","engine","lead","3d",[127,128,129,130],{"_57":121,"_25":122,"_17":116},{"_57":111,"_25":68,"_17":106,"_95":112},{"_57":102,"_25":103,"_95":104,"_156":157},{"_57":93,"_25":94,"_95":96},[155],"ai-assisted","threejs","scope","complete-project",{"_159":160},"documents",{"_161":162,"_163":164},"en",[166,170,171,172,169,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,202,203,204,168,205,167,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220,221,222,223],"zh",[165,166,167,168,169],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools-research","generative-api-boundaries","generation-delivery-contracts","asset-validation-contracts","asset-selection-feedback","visual-evidence-research","visual-feedback-mechanisms","game-development-evaluation","benchmark-reproducibility","gameplay-state-contracts","agent-interface-evidence","catalog-review-coverage","source-revision-notes","community-case-resea